  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), ViperAce throttle grip L Metal 2.0 in its slide-rail frame (no throttle base), seen from the inboard (thumb) side and above, front of the handle to the right: MAN RNG/UNCAGE knob on top, DOG FIGHT and SPD BRK slides, ANT ELEV wheel at the front, RDR CURSOR/ENABLE ministick below",
  "mappingSource": "WinCtrl \"ViperAce Throttle Grip L. Metal 2.0 (VIPER.TG.L.MET.2) User Manual V1.0 2025.11.27\" section 3.2 Key Positions, page 14 (https://eu.winctrl.com/static/ipfs/QmVogWajtbAAa6iTNGjYJBncNX696Loiwywwf3FDMjyL1A), with section 1.1 component names (page 4): 5 + X/Y (6-9) = mini joystick at RDR CURSOR/ENABLE, 10-12 = lower slide (SPD BRK), 13-15 = upper slide (DOG FIGHT), 16/17 + Rz = MAN RNG thumb wheel turned to its ends, 18 = its press (UNCAGE), 19 + Z = ANT ELEV thumb wheel, 23-27 = five-way switch at the top rear (VHF/IFF labels), 3/4 = under-side buttons; matches the catalog numbers",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "All throttle.base.* parts and SLIDER1 belong to the Orion 2 (T2-2) throttle base, which is not on this photo (the grip sits in its slide-rail frame). The five-way switch (23-27) sits on the top rear on the outboard side; only a gray edge of it shows behind the MAN RNG knob, so it is a hidden candidate. The under-side buttons 3/4 face down and are hidden. Catalog issue: throttle.axis.rotary.1 (ANT ELEV) lists JOY_Z and JOY_SLIDER2; the manual gives the ANT ELEV wheel only Z. SLIDER2 is the base's second slider/dial (EDCD 4098BD64 \"Dial\"), not a grip control. The fwd/center/aft order of the slide switches is not stated in the manual (catalog note).",
